 {:seon.task/name "a-stable-prefix-is-sent-once"
  :seon.task/plan "Done: `seon.context/messages` sends [system: the help page, docs/agent.md, the same for every agent] [user: the run's sections (task, plan, references, found helpers, sections, evidence), rendered from the run's first turn's basis] [the scrollback] [user: the turn's sections (turn n of m, proofs, refused, test-run, last reply, unmerged entries, last evaluations, the dropped-turns note)]. The first two messages are byte-identical across a run's turns and nothing is sent twice; DeepSeek and OpenAI-compatible providers cache a byte-identical prefix. Replaced ``seon.context/system-prompt`` and the overflow note's edit of the first message (before, the whole block went out twice a turn and the prefix changed every turn after overflow; notes/archive/AUDIT-v1-to-next-2026-10-22.md 2.3). v1 sent stable run sections in the system message (about 8.5k tokens) and small turn sections (about 0.75k), with 85-91% cache hits. `seon.context/render` stays the one maker; `seon.turn/context-block` shows both user messages."
