(A) The record, at send time. seon.context/request already composes the request from records: the system prompt (the help page), the task story (the run sections), each record of the run kept by the history budget (an eval, :seon.db/eval-fact; a message, :seon.message/fact) by its own :seon.render/ai render, then the screen evals the basis names, and the history note. It answers, beside the messages, the ordered refs they came from: [:text cid] for the system prompt and the task story, [:eval id], [:message id], [:history n]. seon.turn/act! writes them on the turn as it sends (:seon.turn/sent, a vector of refs), with the usage it already records; the two texts once each under their content id (:seon.text/id, the digest of the text, and :seon.text/body; written once, an upsert of the same value writes nothing). New schema: :seon.turn/sent, :seon.text/id, :seon.text/body (root's gate: new attributes). Reuses: request, ai-messages, records, kept, seon.error/digest, the turn record. Deletes: the remake path for later readings (seon.context/remade, run-text, turn-text, recorded; their callers in context_test and e2e read the record instead); reader-text stays only if turn.clj still needs it (checked when building). ~35 lines added, ~60 deleted. Proofs: seon.context-test/a-turn-records-what-it-sent (refs in order, each resolvable), seon.context-test/the-sent-records-are-the-wire-body (for a turn: wire-messages over the messages its refs resolve to, by each record's :seon.render/ai, equals the body seon.model/request-body built and sent, compared as data); cost: seon.context-cost-test/a-turn-records-one-turns-messages (the write is the turn's refs: linear in that turn's messages, flat in the run's earlier turns).
(B) The debug page. /agent/{id}/debug is a view of the agent entity (web view-of `<id>/debug`, as /agent/{id} is), whose page lists the agent's model turns newest first; each turn's row is its :seon.turn/sent refs, each resolved to its record and shown by that record's :seon.render/ai messages through one :seon.render/html render of a sent request (role, content, reasoning folded, each eval call's prose and code, a tool message under its call, the screen evals set apart, tokens and cache hits from the turn's usage, and beside each part the eval, message or text that made it: the owner's 2026-10-24 ruling, \"styled ... show the form and eval result that created it\"). Drawn by the render proc like any page: its walk is recorded (step 2 B'), a new turn touches it (step 2 C), and only the new turn's row renders (units by input). Reuses: render.proc's page path, ui/page's units, the request render's styling from the set-aside jolt/agent-conversation-debug-wip (its hiccup, not its request rebuild). ~70 lines. Proofs: seon.render-test/the-debug-page-shows-what-each-turn-sent (the page's messages for a turn equal the wire body's, as data), seon.render-test/a-new-turn-is-one-new-row (rendered units: one); checked in a browser on this worktree's root with a scripted run.
(C) Cost proof for the page: one new turn costs one turn's messages (renders: the new row only; the walk is the page's, O(turns) until step 4 makes rows their own components, stated in the proof).
